{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2-repair-001\\\\specs\\\\R6_WO-SWOF-W2-R006_SPEC.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# R6 WO-SWOF-W2-R006 — operation / action_class must fail CLOSED (never ungated)\n\nrepair_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R2\nbase: 3ade7d0edec5d3304672be2cfa696e570aaab193   (the R5 candidate)\norigin: my own canonical-domain probe (evidence/R2_UNKNOWN_OPERATION_PROBE.json), verified against the\n        canonical source. Not raised by the external reports; found because R5 fixed the risk/permission/\n        autonomy enum axes but left the OPERATION axis fail-open.\n\n## Canonical law (DOC-03, quoted from a direct read)\n\n- L867: `operation | operation_class / 1 | Y | classifier | Human/view/effect | known action enum |\n  unknown -> UNKNOWN_RUIN/safe-stop`\n- L874: `action_class | enum / 1 | Y | DOC-03 classifier | policy | §09 known class | unknown safe-stop`\n- L396-410: `classify(action)` runs `action_class = classify_operation(action.operation)` and the\n  classification is performed on the EFFECT, \"not on how harmless the prompt text appears\".\n- L627/L1655: profiles carry `allowed_operations: set[operation_class]`.\n- L876: `effect_risk_tier` \"RUIN veto; UNKNOWN safe-stop\".\n\nSo an operation that cannot be classified is NOT benign: it must SAFE-STOP. The \"name may only tighten,\nnever weaken\" rule means an unrecognised name can never be the reason a request is ungated.\n\n## Defect proven at the R5 candidate\n\nWith canonical benign classifications present (LOW/MEDIUM + P0..P2), EVERY operation string is ungated —\nincluding a string that is plainly not a known action:\n\n    operation=\"definitely-not-a-known-operation\" -> required=False, route=\"NONE\", seam=ALLOWED\n    operation=\"unknown_action\"                   -> required=False, route=\"NONE\", seam=ALLOWED\n\nThe `_CLASS_VALID` branch returns the NONE (ungated) route as soon as the classifications are canonically\nbenign, without ever checking that the OPERATION is a known action. Canonically the unknown operation must\nsafe-stop. This is the same fail-open class as the enum defect that R5 fixed, on the one axis R5 left open.\n\n## Required implementation (same seam, smallest change)\n\n1. Introduce a canonical operation/action classification used by the ONE gate predicate:\n   - a set of KNOWN action/operation values, derived from the canonical §09.1 ACTION_EFFECT_CLASS_MATRIX\n     (`ACT-READ-LOCAL`, `ACT-DESIGN-WRITE`, `ACT-EXTERNAL-READ`, `ACT-EXTERNAL-WRITE-REV`,\n     `ACT-EXTERNAL-WRITE-STATEFUL`, `ACT-DATA-EXPORT`, `ACT-SECRET-RESOLVE`, `ACT-IDENTITY-RIGHTS`,\n     `ACT-MERGE`, `ACT-DEPLOY-RELEASE`, `ACT-FINANCIAL`, `ACT-PHYSICAL`, `ACT-DELETE-IRREV`) plus the\n     benign operation names the existing accepted tests already use, so no legitimate control regresses.\n   - an UNCLASSIFIABLE operation (anything not in the known set, or empty / non-string) MUST return the\n     SAFE_STOP route (`RUIN:SAFE_STOP`, i.e. an UNKNOWN_RUIN-classed outcome) — never the NONE route and\n     never ungated.\n2. The classification must be effect-driven: an operation may TIGHTEN the route (a high-risk operation\n   always gates and names its authority edge, already implemented) but an unrecognised operation may\n   NEVER WEAKEN it.\n3. If the canonical operation_class vocabulary cannot be established with confidence for some value,\n   FAIL CLOSED (safe-stop). Over-blocking is acceptable; fail-open is not. Do not guess a benign mapping.\n4. Keep every R5 win intact: canonical EffectRiskTier gating, RUIN/UNKNOWN_RUIN effect-veto precedence,\n   malformed risk/permission/autonomy fail-closed, LOW/MEDIUM + P0/P1/P2 + a KNOWN benign operation\n   remains ungated, RFC8785 JCS + DOMAIN_FRAME + real Ed25519, recomputed approval_basis_hash, exact\n   lineage, mandatory audience, generations, T3 checker evidence, approver != actor.\n\n## Required focused tests\n  operation not in the known action set (any classification) -> SAFE_STOP, never ungated\n  operation=\"\" (empty) and operation=None -> SAFE_STOP\n  a KNOWN benign operation + canonical LOW/MEDIUM + P0/P1/P2 -> remains ungated (positive control)\n  a KNOWN high-risk operation -> gates and names its authority edge (unchanged)\n  all existing R4/R5 tests continue to pass\n\n## write-set\n`src/security/rights.py`, `src/security/humangate.py`, `src/security/tests/test_rights.py`,\n`src/security/tests/test_humangate_currentness.py`. Nothing else. Extend the existing seam; do not add a\nsecond gate/router/authority subsystem.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
