{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath 'C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2-repair-001\\\\specs\\\\R5_WO-SWOF-W2-R005_SPEC.md' -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# R5 WO-SWOF-W2-R005 — canonical EffectRiskTier domain, ruin effect-veto, and fail-closed enums\n\nrepair_id: SWOF-W2-CLOSURE-R2\nbase: edb53142dda94e1b0e4926bebc008b06f42cbcfb  (the R4 candidate)\norigin: fresh-context VERIFY_ONLY checker (blocking finding) + my own decisive re-probe, both grounded in\n        the canonical PI-PKG-06 DOC-03. R4's own probe battery MISSED all of this because its fixtures were\n        built from the implementation's own attribute names instead of the canonical field domains.\n\n## Canonical law (DOC-03, verified by direct read — quote these, do not paraphrase)\n\n`effect_risk_tier` is the canonical EffectRiskTier field. Its enum is\n`[\"LOW\",\"MEDIUM\",\"HIGH\",\"CRITICAL\",\"RUIN\",\"UNKNOWN_RUIN\"]` (DOC-03 line 778, line 876, and the\nApprovalRequest JSON Schema enum at line 1069). `ruin_class` **does not exist anywhere in the canonical\nsource** (0 occurrences). RUIN is carried INSIDE the EffectRiskTier enum.\n\nEffectRiskTier -> HumanGate consequence (DOC-03 lines 441-448):\n- LOW      -> \"P3+ still requires Human token by permission floor\"\n- MEDIUM   -> \"P3 hard binding; HA1/HA2 according deterministic authority matrix\"\n- HIGH     -> \"Human approval + stronger authn; domain coapproval where mapped\"\n- CRITICAL -> \"HA1 + required HA3/HA5; AAC3 authn; safe-stop on ambiguity\"\n- RUIN     -> \"ordinary approval forbidden; HARD_VETO; redesign only\"\n- UNKNOWN_RUIN -> \"TEMP_CLOSED / SAFE_STOP; evidence and bounded reclassification required\"\n\nDOC-03 line 476: \"proposed consequential effect classified RUIN -> `HARD_VETO` regardless of Human token\".\nDOC-03 line 439: the veto attaches to the proposed consequential EFFECT edge, not to a subject-level ruin\nlabel — so P0/P1 read/design over a ruin-class SUBJECT stays admissible (lines 472-474).\nDOC-03 line 489: AutonomyTier T3 \"MUST have explicit Human decision AND independent-checker evidence\".\nDOC-03 §15.6: unknown required enum values must be REJECTED, never coerced.\n\n## Defects proven at the R4 candidate (machine-replayable, see evidence/R2_CANONICAL_RUIN_PROBE.json)\n\nD1 [BLOCKING, FAIL-OPEN] A canonical request with `effect_risk_tier=\"RUIN\"` and a VALID token returns\n   \"allowed\" (no refusal). The gate reads ruin ONLY from a `ruin_class` attribute that is not canonical, so\n   a canonically-classified RUIN effect does not veto. With no token it raises the wrong code\n   (`NOT_A_CANONICAL_APPROVAL_TOKEN`) instead of `HARD_VETO_RUIN`. Same for `UNKNOWN_RUIN`.\n\nD2 [BLOCKING] The risk-tier half of the gate is dead: `effect_risk_tier` is compared against\n   {\"P3\",\"P4\",\"P5\"}, which are PERMISSION class values, not EffectRiskTier values. Canonical\n   `CRITICAL`/`HIGH` (and `MEDIUM`) therefore do not gate. The permission_class branch still denies, so the\n   headline P3 case is not open — but the claimed risk-tier rule is vacuous.\n\nD3 [BLOCKING] Malformed/unknown enum values fail OPEN: `permission_class` in {\"p3\",\"P3 \",\" P3\",\"\",\"P9\"}\n   is treated as ungated. §15.6 requires rejection.\n\nD4 [NON-BLOCKING, fix in the same cone] AutonomyTier is not an input to the gate predicate; T3 must\n   require a Human decision + checker evidence.\n\nD5 [NON-BLOCKING] `verify_approval_token` can raise AttributeError instead of returning a typed decision\n   when `ctx.nonce_ledger` is a non-None object lacking `.reserve()`.\n\nD6 [NON-BLOCKING] `human_gate_route(\"\")` returns required=True (unknown_action) while\n   `human_gate_required(ApprovalRequest(operation=\"\"))` returns required=False — the \"ONE canonical\n   predicate\" invariant is violated.\n\n## Required implementation (smallest existing-seam change; NO second router/authority system)\n\n1. Introduce the canonical EffectRiskTier domain in ONE place:\n   `EFFECT_RISK_TIERS = (\"LOW\",\"MEDIUM\",\"HIGH\",\"CRITICAL\",\"RUIN\",\"UNKNOWN_RUIN\")`.\n2. Ruin precedence is derived from the canonical field:\n   `effect_risk_tier == \"RUIN\"` -> HARD_VETO (code `HARD_VETO_RUIN`);\n   `effect_risk_tier == \"UNKNOWN_RUIN\"` -> SAFE_STOP (code `SAFE_STOP_UNKNOWN_RUIN`).\n   Evaluated FIRST, before schema/binding/signature/approval; a valid token may NOT override either.\n   `ruin_class` may be accepted as a LEGACY ALIAS only if the canonical field is absent, and the alias must\n   never weaken the canonical value. Document the alias as non-canonical.\n3. Token requirement (the single canonical predicate), fail-closed:\n   require a valid exact-bound Human ApprovalToken if ANY of:\n     - `effect_risk_tier` in {\"HIGH\",\"CRITICAL\",\"RUIN\",\"UNKNOWN_RUIN\"}   (canonical risk tiers)\n     - `permission_class` in {\"P3\",\"P4\",\"P5\"}\n     - `autonomy_tier == \"T3\"`\n     - the operation maps to an explicit high-risk HumanGate authority edge\n   Operation name may TIGHTEN or identify the route; it may never WEAKEN any of the above.\n   `effect_risk_tier` in {\"LOW\",\"MEDIUM\"} does NOT by itself require a token (the permission floor and the\n   autonomy axis still may) — this is the required low-risk positive control.\n4. FAIL CLOSED on unknown enum values: a `permission_class`, `effect_risk_tier` or `autonomy_tier` that is\n   present but NOT a member of its canonical set, or malformed (`\"p3\"`, `\"P3 \"`, `\"P9\"`, `\"\"`), must be\n   REFUSED (DENY/SAFE-STOP) — never coerced and never treated as ungated. Absent (None) is distinct from\n   present-but-invalid; an absent classification on an operation that requires one must also fail closed.\n5. Unify the two entry points so `human_gate_route(\"\")` and `human_gate_required(...)` agree; the\n   unknown-operation rule must live in the ONE canonical predicate.\n6. `verify_approval_token` must return a typed decision for a malformed `nonce_ledger` (never raise).\n7. Keep the R4 wins intact: RFC8785 JCS, DOMAIN_FRAME, real Ed25519 over the framed bytes, recomputed\n   approval_basis_hash, exact request/decision lineage, mandatory audience, generation bindings,\n   T3 independent-checker evidence, no approver==actor.\n\n## Required focused tests (first-failing -> repair -> PASS)\n\n  effect_risk_tier=\"RUIN\" + valid token -> HARD_VETO_RUIN\n  effect_risk_tier=\"RUIN\" + no token   -> HARD_VETO_RUIN\n  effect_risk_tier=\"UNKNOWN_RUIN\" + valid token -> SAFE_STOP_UNKNOWN_RUIN\n  effect_risk_tier=\"CRITICAL\" + P2 + benign op + no token -> token REQUIRED\n  effect_risk_tier=\"HIGH\" + P2 + benign op + no token -> token REQUIRED\n  effect_risk_tier=\"LOW\"/\"MEDIUM\" + P2 + benign op -> remains ungated (positive control)\n  permission_class in {\"p3\",\"P3 \",\" P3\",\"\",\"P9\"} -> REFUSED, not ungated\n  effect_risk_tier in {\"p3\",\"ruin\",\"\"} -> REFUSED, not ungated\n  autonomy_tier=\"T3\" + benign op + no token -> token REQUIRED + checker evidence required\n  human_gate_route(\"\") and human_gate_required(operation=\"\") AGREE\n  malformed nonce_ledger -> typed decision, no exception raised\n  all R4 regression tests continue to pass\n\n## Constraints\n- write-set: `src/security/rights.py`, `src/security/humangate.py`,\n  `src/security/tests/test_rights.py`, `src/security/tests/test_humangate_currentness.py`,\n  `schemas/security/approval_token.schema.json`. Nothing else. Do not touch other W2 substrates.\n- no second gate/router/authority subsystem; extend the existing seam.\n- do not weaken any existing refusal; every change must be neutral-or-stricter.\n- do not edit tests to match code; the canonical enum domain above is the authority.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
